cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite the manuscript and its exact reproducibility package."
type: article
title: "Full-Dimensional Jukes-Cantor Ambiguity in Weakly Tree-Child Level-2 Networks"
authors:
  - family-names: Kriebel
    given-names: Alec
date-released: 2026-08-09
version: 2.0.0-rc1
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/tree/main/s_tc_jc_sharp_boundary"
abstract: >-
  For every n at least four, two nonisomorphic and non-triangle-equivalent
  binary level-2 semi-directed networks that are weakly but not strongly
  tree-child have Jukes-Cantor model images with a common regular
  full-dimensional stochastic region of dimension 2n.
